# Spec 07 Phase C — ISP curated cards (PERIPHERY)
#
# ACCEPTANCE CONTRACT (written before edits)
# C1 GIVEN functions/ispPlansData.json, WHEN its validator loads the seed, THEN
#    Google Fiber, AT&T Fiber, Xfinity, Spectrum, and T-Mobile Home Internet each
#    have a unique real plan with speed, price, promo, contract, provider URL,
#    one why-line, research date, and an official source recorded in the file.
# C2 GIVEN Adam's CJ/Impact links are absent, WHEN a plan uses the literal
#    #AFFILIATE_PENDING placeholder, THEN the client logs the open item and opens
#    the HTTPS provider URL in-app; the placeholder is never parsed as a URL.
# C3 GIVEN an authenticated user opens SETUP_INTERNET, WHEN the flow loads, THEN
#    it reads ispPlans from Firestore, loads the user's canonical new address,
#    shows "Plans for {city/zip}", and renders ordered reusable comparison cards
#    with provider, speed, price, promo, contract, and one why-line.
# C4 GIVEN a rendered plan card, WHEN the user taps it, THEN SFSafariViewController
#    opens the affiliate URL when present or the provider URL otherwise, and the
#    user can mark the task complete after the handoff.
# C5 GIVEN Firestore or identity loading fails, WHEN the flow renders, THEN it
#    provides an accessible retry/fallback state without changing the catalog or
#    claiming address-level serviceability; all new controls have stable ids and
#    44-point targets and the simulator build succeeds.
# C6 GIVEN the completed Phase C implementation and seed validator, WHEN a fresh-
#    context validator runs, THEN C1-C5 receive evidence-backed PASS/FAIL before
#    the sanctioned ispPlans seed runs; after seeding, round-trip plus authenticated
#    read-back provide live evidence before Phase C closes.
#
# NEEDS-CLARIFICATION (bounded, reversible interpretations)
# - No CJ/Impact ISP links exist in the repository, so every plan stores
#   affiliateURL:"#AFFILIATE_PENDING" and a separate official providerURL. This
#   is the spec's explicit graceful-degradation path and remains an open item.
# - No serviceability API is permitted in v1. Curated cards are KC-area candidates,
#   never address-qualified claims; every provider handoff performs its own check.
# - The shared ComparisonCardView is mover-worded internally. Reuse its model/view
#   while supplying ISP-specific field labels through a small optional label
#   adapter so existing mover call sites remain byte-for-byte behavior compatible.
